.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:1:# Pi-goals live probe agent testing
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:3:This document is the canonical project-local guide for validating `pi-goal` behavior in a real Pi interactive session through Solo. It complements deterministic probes and `npm run quality:goal`; it does not replace them.
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:7:Use the live probe surface when a `pi-goal` change affects behavior that only becomes trustworthy in the real Pi TUI/agent loop, such as:
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:9:- slash-command dispatch and autocomplete interactions;
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:10:- goal widget/status rendering and notifications;
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:15:A live probe is usually expected for behavior-changing fixes in `pi-goals` unless the user explicitly says not to run one.
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:41:pi-goals-live-probe
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:49:SOLO_INSTANCE="${SOLO_INSTANCE:-solo-pi_goals}"
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:53:solo-mcp --instance "$SOLO_INSTANCE" process status pi-goals-live-probe --project "$SOLO_PROJECT"
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:56:If status-by-name is unsupported in the installed CLI, list processes and select the running process named `pi-goals-live-probe`; store its id in a shell variable for the current validation only:
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:65:PROBE_PROCESS="pi-goals-live-probe"
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:70:Only spawn a new probe when no suitable existing `pi-goals-live-probe` process is alive.
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:72:Use a Pi runtime agent process named `pi-goals-live-probe` in the current project:
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:75:SOLO_INSTANCE="${SOLO_INSTANCE:-solo-pi_goals}"
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:82:  --name pi-goals-live-probe
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:85:After spawning, wait until the process is ready before sending commands. Check status/output rather than assuming immediate readiness:
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:88:solo-mcp --instance "$SOLO_INSTANCE" process status pi-goals-live-probe --project "$SOLO_PROJECT"
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:89:solo-mcp --instance "$SOLO_INSTANCE" process output pi-goals-live-probe --project "$SOLO_PROJECT" --lines 80
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:97:solo-mcp --instance "$SOLO_INSTANCE" process send "$PROBE_PROCESS" --project "$SOLO_PROJECT" --input '/goal queue count to five'
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:103:- For single slash-command inputs, the local `solo-mcp` CLI sends a follow-up raw Enter after a 500ms delay to handle Pi autocomplete consuming the first Enter.
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:113:solo-mcp --instance "$SOLO_INSTANCE" process send "$PROBE_PROCESS" --project "$SOLO_PROJECT" --input '/goal queue count to five'
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:118:Some `/goal` paths can open a TUI confirmation such as Replace / Queue / Cancel when a goal already exists.
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:128:For stale prompt text, autocomplete overlays, or accidental partial input, prefer clearing the editor before the next scripted command:
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:153:Use this when validating queue steering or `/goal resume` behavior:
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:156:solo-mcp --instance "$SOLO_INSTANCE" process send "$PROBE_PROCESS" --project "$SOLO_PROJECT" --input '/goal clear'
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:158:solo-mcp --instance "$SOLO_INSTANCE" process send "$PROBE_PROCESS" --project "$SOLO_PROJECT" --input '/goal queue count to five'
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:160:solo-mcp --instance "$SOLO_INSTANCE" process send "$PROBE_PROCESS" --project "$SOLO_PROJECT" --input '/goal resume'
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:165:Expected evidence for no-active-goal resume:
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:167:- `No active goal. Resuming queued goal processing for 1 queued goal.`
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:168:- `start_queued_goal` starts the queued item.
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:169:- the queued goal objective is completed.
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:171:To validate completed-goal resume, leave a completed current goal, enqueue another goal, then run `/goal resume`:
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:174:solo-mcp --instance "$SOLO_INSTANCE" process send "$PROBE_PROCESS" --project "$SOLO_PROJECT" --input '/goal queue count to five'
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:176:solo-mcp --instance "$SOLO_INSTANCE" process send "$PROBE_PROCESS" --project "$SOLO_PROJECT" --input '/goal resume'
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:183:- `Goal is complete. Resuming queued goal processing for 1 queued goal.`
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:184:- `start_queued_goal` starts the queued item.
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:185:- the queued goal objective is completed.
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:190:solo-mcp --instance "$SOLO_INSTANCE" process send "$PROBE_PROCESS" --project "$SOLO_PROJECT" --input '/goal queue'
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:197:A live probe is complete only when the transcript or output shows the behavior under test. Good evidence includes:
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:202:- final queue/goal state when relevant.
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:208:- Prefer existing `pi-goals-live-probe`; do not spawn duplicate probe agents casually.
.ai/docs/pi-goals-live-probe-testing.md:213:- Clean up goals/queues deliberately. Do not discard queued work without explicit authorization or a satisfied queue head.
