./AGENTS.md:26:npm run quality:goal
./AGENTS.md:58:Live probes complement deterministic tests; they do not replace `npm run quality:goal` or targeted probes. For a small change with direct, unambiguous deterministic coverage, the live probe may be skipped to save time/tokens, but provide a visible reason in the current closeout context.
./package.json:4:  "description": "Persistent goal tracking for Pi with /tree-compatible state, budgets, reusable prompts, and churn monitoring.",
./package.json:14:    "quality:goal": "sentrux gate .pi/extensions/goal && sentrux check .pi/extensions/goal && npm run slop:goal && npm run typecheck:goal && pi --offline --no-session --no-tools -e .pi/extensions/goal/index.ts --list-models >/tmp/pi-goal-quality-load.txt"
./README.md:3:Persistent goal tracking for [Pi](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent). Inspired by Codex CLI's `/goal`, `pi-goals` adds Pi-native UX, rewindable `/tree`-compatible goal state, time and token budgets, reusable token-aware prompts, automated churn monitoring, and more.
./README.md:11:- Time and token budgets with goal-aware continuation and wrap-up behavior.
./README.md:50:- `/goal` — show the current goal summary, status, budgets, and progress metadata.
./README.md:91:Set a goal to finish the README cleanup with a 30 minute budget, then keep going until it is done or blocked.
./README.md:100:When a goal reaches its time or token budget, `pi-goals` steers the agent into wrap-up instead of silently continuing. Exhausted goals cannot be resumed until the budget is raised or the goal is cleared.
./README.md:159:npm run quality:goal
./README.md:162:`npm run quality:goal` runs the project quality gate for the extension, including [Sentrux](https://github.com/sentrux/sentrux) structure checks, TypeScript validation, and Pi extension load validation.

