.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/08-bcu-chatgpt-research.md:1676:## Round 3 concrete findings to carry forward
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/08-bcu-chatgpt-research.md:1680:3. **Same-call floor removal plus completion is not a first-release escape hatch.** A single `update_goal` call must not both lower/remove an unmet floor and set `status:"complete"`; first release requires two calls so the gate evaluates current persisted floors.
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/08-bcu-chatgpt-research.md:1684:7. **Strict tool input, defensive replay.** Tool schemas should reject malformed floor fields, but replay/loading should treat missing or malformed optional historical floor fields as absent instead of crashing state reconstruction.
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/08-bcu-chatgpt-research.md:1686:9. **Monitor floor telemetry needs stale guards.** Apply floor-pattern telemetry mutations only when the report goal id still matches the current active goal and `floor.completionBlockedByFloor` is true.
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/08-bcu-chatgpt-research.md:1691:## Round 3 maintainer invariant excerpt
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/08-bcu-chatgpt-research.md:1697:Round 3B produced a final invariant list worth carrying into the issue doc:
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/08-bcu-chatgpt-research.md:1700:- Completion floors are evaluated against the current persisted goal, not a candidate goal already edited to remove/lower floors or set status:"complete".
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/08-bcu-chatgpt-research.md:1705:- Max token/time budgets always override min floors; budget-limited wrap-up must not schedule or prompt floor-value work.
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/08-bcu-chatgpt-research.md:1710:- createGoalState must use a named options object for max budgets and min floors.
