.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/03-design-lock.md:67:Update-tool parameters additionally allow `null` to remove a configured floor, matching existing max-budget edit semantics. A single `update_goal` call must not both remove/lower an unmet completion floor and set `status:"complete"`; first release requires two separate updates so the gate evaluates current persisted floors.
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/03-design-lock.md:90:- Completion remains allowed for an actually complete `budgetLimited` goal only if the floor gate is satisfied; otherwise the user can clear/lower floors or accept the budget-limited wrap-up as incomplete progress.
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/03-design-lock.md:91:- `buildBudgetLimitPrompt(...)` and budget-limited continuation paths must not ask the worker to choose floor-value passes; budget wrap-up summarizes progress and max-budget state rather than trying to satisfy floors.
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/03-design-lock.md:119:Also change `createGoalState` to accept a named options object (`objective`, max budgets, min floors, optional `now`) rather than adding more optional positional arguments; this avoids silent argument swaps across create/template/queue paths.
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/03-design-lock.md:224:Floor-related monitor decisions may mutate floor telemetry only when the report goal id still matches the current active goal and `floor.completionBlockedByFloor` is true. Stale monitor floor patterns must not poison telemetry after the goal is complete, paused, budget-limited, absent, or no longer floor-blocked.
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/03-design-lock.md:243:- State/types for floors, with strict tool validation and defensive replay that treats missing or malformed optional historical floor fields as absent instead of crashing.
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/03-design-lock.md:276:- same-call floor removal/lowering plus `status:"complete"` bypasses the current persisted floor gate;
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/03-design-lock.md:282:- maximum budgets can be bypassed by minimum floors or budget-limited prompts ask for more floor work;
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/03-design-lock.md:286:- stale monitor floor decisions mutate telemetry after the goal is no longer current and floor-blocked;
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/03-design-lock.md:287:- replay of malformed optional floor fields crashes state reconstruction;
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/04-proof-threat-model.md:10:- Floors are persisted/replayed through goal and queue state without breaking old sessions that lack the optional fields; malformed optional floor fields in replay are ignored/sanitized rather than crashing.
.ai/docs/issue-workflow/ISSUE-036-minimum-goal-spend-floors/04-proof-threat-model.md:24:   - A min floor causes the agent to continue after token/time maximum budgets are exhausted, or budget-limited wrap-up prompts ask for floor-value work.
